r hands will call or raise. There is very little "thin value" to be had. Therefore, the best move is to check back, realize my equity, and hopefully win the pot at showdown without risking more chips.\n\nReason: The opponent has shown weakness by checking every round. While my Two Pair is likely good, betting is unlikely to get called by a worse hand on this texture, and it risks losing more to a slow-played Ace or Eight. Checking secures the showdown and maximizes the chance of winning the current pot safely.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
