s losses if I am behind, and allows me to see the Turn card potentially for free to hit an Ace or a 4.\n2. **Bet (100):** Betting into a limped pot acts as a bluff. While it might fold out some equity from the opponent, it bloats the pot while I am out of position with a hand that is currently just High Card.\n3. **Fold (-1):** There is no bet to call, so folding is irrational as checking costs nothing.\n\nReason:\nI have Ace-High, which is often the best hand in a limped pot where the opponent showed no aggression pre-flop. However, it is not strong enough to bet for value because worse hands will fold and better hands will call. Being out of position, checking allows me to control the pot size and realize my equity (potentially hitting a pair or winning with Ace-high at showdown) without risking more chips unnecessarily.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
